  "extra_findings": [
    "Visibility rule not enforced in the listing and CSV export: any client lists and exports every client's tickets (index.php:72-74, lib.php:132). Reported as F1 (listing part) and F4; the matrix plants only the ?ver= IDOR.",
    "Session cookie issued without HttpOnly/SameSite (index.php:15). Bundled into F10 with SEC-013.",
    "exportarCsv writes to a fixed shared path, EXPORT_DIR/chamados.csv (lib.php:125-126): concurrent exports can truncate each other, a copy of every ticket stays on disk, and a missing directory yields an empty HTTP 200 (F8).",
    "Integer ids concatenated into SQL in tecnicoNome (lib.php:69) and verChamado (lib.php:100). Not exploitable given the int typing and the report says so; hardening only (F11).",
    "formatarStatus maps any status other than 1/2 to 'Resolvido' (lib.php:32-33), which would misclassify out-of-range values (F13).",
    "Array-valued request parameters (busca[]=x, login[]=x) raise a TypeError and HTTP 500 at index.php:22 and :73 (F14).",
    "SEC-005: no CSRF token or rate limiting on the login POST. Mentioned in Decisions §3.4, not changed."
  ],
